# Copy to `.env` and fill in the values. `.env` is gitignored.
#
# The starter runs without any of these set — the dev-mode admin
# picks from two hardcoded test accounts in src/access/index.ts.
# Set `SEED_ADMIN_ID` the first time you want to log in as admin;
# after your first login, the env is ignored (the role assignment
# persists in storage). See docs/seeding-the-first-admin.md.

# --- Access (dev) ---

# Identity id that becomes the first admin on first login. For
# dev this is one of the test-account ids from src/access/index.ts
# (`admin@local` or `viewer@local`). For production with a real
# auth adapter (Google / OIDC / Apple) it's whatever the adapter
# surfaces as `identity.id` — often an email, sometimes a subject
# claim.
SEED_ADMIN_ID=admin@local

# --- Access (production, when you swap adapters) ---

# Google OAuth 2.0 client id. Only needed if you replace the dev
# test-accounts adapter with `createGoogleAuthAdapter`. See
# docs/add-google-auth.md.
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com

# --- Hosting (deployment only) ---

# The canonical origin — used in sitemap, canonical URLs, and
# `Astro.site` computations. Astro defaults to localhost during
# dev; set this for deployed builds.
# SITE=https://yourdomain.com
